<title>USA: CBOE to list eight new equity options.</title>
<headline>CBOE to list eight new equity options.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board Options Exchange (CBOE) said Wednesday it would list options on seven companies on February 28 and on one other company on March 3.</p>
<p>Options on Cox Radio Inc, Einstein/Noah Bagel Corp, First Financial Corp of Wisconsin, PFF Bancorp, Paxson Communications Corp, Sawtek Inc and American Depositary Shares (ADSs) of UK-based Energy Group Plc, will begin trading February 28, the CBOE said.</p>
<p>Options on American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) of Venezuela's CANTV will open March 3. </p>
<p>The following table lists the stocks' ticker symbols, the options' strike prices, exercise months and trading crowd or designated primary market maker (DPM). The following six options will begin trading February 28:</p>
<p>    Strikes	 Months	Crowd/DPM</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    15, 17-1/2,   Mar, Apr,   Wal-Mart Stores crowd</p>
<p>	     20		Jul, Oct</p>
<p>   22-1/2, 25,   Mar, Apr,   O.T.A. LP</p>
<p>	     30		May, Aug</p>
<p>   25, 30, 35    Mar, Apr,   Susquehanna Inv Group</p>
<p>				 Jun, Sep</p>
<p>   12-1/2, 15,   Mar, Apr,   Hewlett-Packard crowd</p>
<p>	     17-1/2	  May, Aug</p>
<p>    7-1/2, 10,    Mar, Apr,   TFM Investment Group</p>
<p>	     12-1/2	  Jun, Sep</p>
<p>   30, 35, 40    Mar, Apr,   Texas Instruments crowd</p>
<p>				 Jun, Sep</p>
<p>    30, 35, 40    Mar, Apr,   Viacom Class B crowd</p>
<p>				 Jun, Sep</p>
<p>The following option will begin trading March 3:</p>
<p>    25, 30, 35    Mar, Apr,   General Motors crowd</p>
<p>				 Jul, Oct</p>
<p>((--Derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
